# check runs every spec in the specs directory and exits 1 if one has an error.
cd $EXAMPLES/refund
exits 1 sv check
cmp stdout $WORK/all.txt
! stderr .

# The JSON format has the same findings.
exits 1 sv check --format json
cmp stdout $WORK/all.json

# check takes spec files as arguments. A passing spec exits 0.
exits 0 sv check specs/ORD-142.yaml
cmp stdout $WORK/one.txt

# Flags can come after the file arguments.
exits 1 sv check specs/ORD-144.yaml --format json
stdout '"rule": "SV001"'

# An unknown format is a usage error.
exits 2 sv check --format yaml
! stdout .
stderr '^invalid value "yaml" for flag -format: unknown format "yaml"; use text or json$'
! stderr '^sv:'

# A missing spec file is an error.
exits 2 sv check specs/nope.yaml
stderr 'specs/nope.yaml: open .*specs/nope.yaml: no such file or directory'

-- one.txt --
specval checked 1 spec(s) and found 0 error(s) and 0 warning(s).
-- all.txt --
specs/ORD-143.yaml:8 error SV107 No call covers AC2 (acceptance[1])
    fix: Add AC2 to `covers` on the call(s) that implement it, or add the missing call.
specs/ORD-143.yaml:10 error SV109 ShippingManager is not a registered service (services.changed[1])
    fix: If ShippingManager is new, move it to services.new with a layer and purpose. Otherwise use a registered service: OrderManager.
specs/ORD-143.yaml:14 error ORD001 OrderAccessor cannot call PricingEngine (calls[2])
    fix: Make OrderManager call PricingEngine, and give the price to the services that need it.
specs/ORD-143.yaml:14 error SV102 OrderAccessor (accessor) cannot call PricingEngine (engine) (calls[2])
    fix: Accessors can call only resources and utilities. Send the call to PricingEngine through a manager.
specs/ORD-143.yaml:15 error SV101 RefundEngine is not a registered service (calls[3].to)
    fix: If RefundEngine is new, declare it under services.new with a layer and purpose. Otherwise use a registered service: PricingEngine.
specs/ORD-143.yaml:15 error SV108 AC4 is not an acceptance criterion in this spec (calls[3].covers[1])
    fix: Use one of: AC1, AC2, or add AC4 under acceptance.
specs/ORD-144.yaml:1 error SV001 acceptance is required
    fix: Add `acceptance`: The acceptance criteria. Give one or more, and make each one possible to test.
specs/ORD-144.yaml:1 error SV001 calls is required
    fix: Add `calls`: Each call from one service to another that this change adds or changes.
specs/ORD-144.yaml:1 error SV001 kind is required
    fix: Add `kind`: The kind of change: feature, bugfix, or chore.
specs/ORD-144.yaml:1 error SV001 summary is required
    fix: Add `summary`: A short paragraph that tells the problem and the new behavior.
specs/ORD-144.yaml:1 error SV001 Additional property cals is not allowed
    fix: Remove `cals`, or correct its name. The permitted fields here are: acceptance, calls, id, kind, out_of_scope, services, specval, status, summary, title.
specs/ORD-144.yaml:2 error SV001 Does not match pattern '^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$' (id)
    fix: Correct the value of `id`. The ID of the ticket, for example ORD-142. Use letters, digits, '.', '_', and '-'. Name the spec file <id>.yaml.
specval checked 3 spec(s) and found 12 error(s) and 0 warning(s).
